        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/858c86/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-07-10T16:48:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>(I know I'm supposed to submit bugs through the app, but I wanted to post the situation here to make sure it's a bug before I waste the good folks at Handelabra's time)</p><p>Grandpa Legacy, Mr. Fixer, Argent Adept, Unity, and Dark Visionary vs. The Ennead in the Tomb of Anubis. &nbsp;Heroic Interception is in play.</p><p>Mr. Fixer has Jack Handle and Alternating Tiger Claw in play. &nbsp;An ankh card is played and Osiris forces each hero to deal themself 1 Psychic damage. &nbsp;Legacy does, then the other four heroes should be immune, right? &nbsp;When Mr. Fixer attempts to deal himself 1 Psychic damage, Jack Handle kicks in and he instead deals 2 Irreducible damage to each non-Hero target. &nbsp;(Two damage because he has Twist the Ether on him, if that matters.)</p><p><span>If I was playing this myself, I would assume that Mr. Fixer would not deal damage to himself due to Heroic Interception and thus Jack Handle would not kick in. &nbsp;Is this a bug that I should submit or am I just playing it wrong at home?&nbsp;</span></p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:45:02.169Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
